liba52 for ac3.library: where it came from, and what was changed
=================================================================

Source: a52dec 0.8.0 (5 November 2022, the release that took over the
unreleased 0.7.5 work, maintained since at VideoLAN), from Adelie Linux's
import, github.com/jsaowji/a52dec at commit 2d6d121 (which adds Alpine's
gcc 15 patch). code.videolan.org and the release tarball's mirrors could
not be reached from the build machine, so the files were not compared with
the official a52dec-0.8.0.tar.gz (MD5 4debeed0257f5312e84d92711a5cfcec
according to Linux From Scratch). Only liba52's decoder (liba52/*.c, *.h)
and its public headers (include/a52.h, attributes.h, mm_accel.h) are kept,
with COPYING, AUTHORS, README and NEWS; the a52dec program, libao and the
build system are left out.

Licence: GPL-2.0-or-later (COPYING), as all of liba52.

Changes (14 November 2026, for ac3.library):

1. liba52/a52_internal.h: a third choice of the fixed-point build's
   multiplies, A52_MUL64: the full 32 x 32 -> 64-bit product shifted, one
   MULS.L on a 68020, 68030 or 68040 (not the 68060, which has no 64-bit
   MULS.L and would trap to 68060.library), else the same in 64-bit C. The
   results are the 64-bit C's on every machine. It halves the decoding time
   on a 68020 against upstream's default (three 16-bit products), and is
   more accurate.

2. liba52/imdct.c: A52_IMDCT_TABLES and A52_IMDCT_DUMP. With
   A52_IMDCT_DUMP, a52_imdct_dump() writes the IMDCT's tables (the window,
   the FFT roots and the twiddle factors) as C; with A52_IMDCT_TABLES
   naming that file, a52_imdct_init() copies them instead of computing
   them with sin, cos, sqrt and a Bessel function in double precision. The
   tables are made on the build host (src/ac3lib/mktables.c), so the Amiga
   needs no floating point and no maths library when a decoder is opened.
   Without either macro the file is as it was.
